{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ואשר הוא עושה ה' מצליח", :translit "v'asher hu oseh Hashem matzliach", :gloss "and whatever he did, YHWH made it prosper"} {:he "מצליח", :translit "matzliach", :gloss "makes prosper"} {:he "בידו", :translit "b'yado", :gloss "in his hand"} {:he "בבית האסורים", :translit "b'veit ha'asurim", :gloss "in the house of prisoners"} {:he "למעלה", :translit "l'ma'alah", :gloss "above"} {:he "בית אדוניו", :translit "beit adonav", :gloss "his master's house"} {:he "של אדוניו", :translit "shel adonav", :gloss "of his master"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Contrast with identical phrase at Genesis 39:3 which adds בידו; here the word is absent"}], :frame {:text "At Genesis 39:3, the parallel statement about Joseph reads וכל אשר הוא עושה ה' מצליח בידו, 'and whatever he did, YHWH made it prosper in his hand,' while here at Genesis 39:23 the phrase בידו is absent. The Ba'al HaTurim accounts for the difference by context: in Potiphar's house (Genesis 39:2–6) Joseph was physically active in his master's affairs, whereas in the prison his circumstances were different.", :sources ["Genesis 39:3" "Genesis 39:23"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Contrast with identical phrase at Genesis 39:3 which adds בידו; here the word is absent", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:10:52.878732370Z", :model "glm-5.2"}